      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Dedetanuq|400190\", \"verdict\": \"same_name\", \"reasoning\": \"Transliteration Dd.t-Ꜥnq.t reads as d, d, t | ꜥ, n, q, t. In Dedetanuq: d = D; d = the second d, with the e between as an extra vowel letter; t = t, with the following a as the next sign. ꜥ = the vowel letter a, which sits between t (the neighbour on the left) and n (the neighbour on the right). n = n; the u is an extra vowel letter standing for no sign; q = q. The final t, which ends the element and the name, is the feminine ending and may be left out. Every sign is matched in order and no consonant of Dedetanuq is left over, so the two spellings are the same name (Dedet-Anqet/Anukis).\"}"
